 came from all over the globe to  add flair and pizzazz to these big dance  routines and in the main cast members  and you've got magic choreographers  exclaimed that descendants opening  number rotten to the core had a dirty  gritty 70s funk dance feel to it it was  aggressive and unapologetically rotten  it had come out with a big bang because  it set the tone for the whole movie  dan sequence in d2 titled you and me  took place on a completely flooded yacht  deck water splashed around cast members  with every dance move this wicked cool  dance number required two huge water  cannons to spray the area the payoff was  huge  that number is totally unforgettable pre  filming Chan it's no secret that the  cast has become incredibly close during  the filming of all three descendants  films they've laughed a lot they've  cried they pranked each other and yes  they've become a family over the five  years they've spent working on  descendants movies of course when you're  that close inside jokes and special  rituals are bound to develop sophia  carson in the cast shared a special  behind-the-scenes secret about the pre  shooting ritual they performed before  each big musical number director Kenny  Ortega taught the cast a chant to get  them hyped up and ready to give it their  all in front of the cameras all the  dancers and all the cast would huddle up  into a big circle and do this chant  together china anne mcclain said it  helped the whole cast get amped before a  scene we're gonna go out on a limb and  say it totally worked  the musical numbers are full of energy  the dance routines are masterful and fun  and the billing kids add their own flair  of sass and passion to each musical  number who knew the power of boom  Shakalaka could be so incredible like  father like daughter Celia is one of the  coolest villain kids on the aisle she's  the daughter of doctor facili a this  girl has got some tricks up her sleeve  she's quick with a card trick and an  evil laugh and she's got a spooky sense  of style looking at her it's safe to say  she's a total daddy's girl at the Disney  fan fest actress who plays the role of  Celia Jada Marie revealed some  interesting details about her character  she said that Celia is 100% a daddy's  girl she added that Celia is a  mischievous little thing  according to her Celia is all about the  cash just like her dad for those of us  who have been speculating from the d3  trailers on whether Celia will be good  or evil this is a pretty big giveaway  but will Celia follow in her dad's  footsteps for good where will she go on  the same path as the og villain kids and  change her wicked ways  we know that then wanted to bring the  villain kids to Oregon but surely not  all of them are ready to let go of their  evil family history  maybe Celia is one of those characters  who remains rotten to the core  daddy blue hair Cheyenne Jackson plays  the role of Hades in descendant three  from the exclusive Hades trailer that  Disney released it's clear that he's got  a score to settle with felon B's Hades  feels this way because they decided long  ago to cast out those who didn't fit the  auradon mold he says that they forced  everyone who didn't agree with them away  to a crowded little island with no magic  no freedom and no hope then he added  that there's only so long you can be in  a place like that before it drives you  to madness or makes you hungry for  revenge but thanks to the king and queen  of auradon he has been relegated to the  lord of the underground and he's kinda  grumpy about it during the disney fan  fest Cheyenne Jackson shared that  playing this villain was a super fun  experience Cheyenne is a parent of two  year old twins he shared that when his  kids came to see him on set they weren't  mesmerised by his blue hair fans in the  crowd laughed when Cheyenne mentioned  that his kids called him daddy blue hair  my daddy blue hair that's very funny  the crew kicked them out dub Cameron and  Sofia Carson have been best friend gold  since the very first descendants movie  they've been through so much together it  makes sense that they wouldn't want the  filming of the last descendants movie to  end the memories they shared will surely  last a lifetime dub cameron shared that  one of her favorite memories occurred  during the last day of shooting their  last musical number in descendants three  sofia chimed in and shared that that was  purely coincidental because usually when  you shoot a movie you shoot out of order  but it just so happened that they shot  the final number on their last day dub  said that everyone in the cast was  really emotional because they all loved  the musical numbers so much they just  didn't want it to end so Devin Sophia  stayed long after filming head wrapped  he said they laid down on the ground of  the set with this massive green screen  until they were told that they had to  leave they stayed so long that the crew  had to kick them out but before they  went they shared a few laughs and a few  tears  so did a lot of reminiscing and took a  ton of photos late night grocery run  when you're busy filming a major Disney  Channel Original Movie it's easy to get  completely consumed by it all we  imagined there wasn't a lot of time for  the normal day-to-day stuff like grocery  shoppings booboo Stewart kind of  confirmed this when he shared his  favorite memory on the Disney fan fest  stage he said that one of his favorite  memories was the night that the cast  went out on a late-night grocery run in  their robes the night that they wrapped  production of descendant 3 a bunch of  the cast members went to the grocery  store in their roads that they took from  the set he stocked up on all the snacks  and delicious food they had been craving  they packed up their grocery store  goodies and crowded into one hotel room  where they completely picked out dub  revealed that more tears were shed that  night as well when you form deep  friendships like these you're bound to  wind up crying with a mouth full of ice  cream together at one point or another  saying goodbye it the film came to a  close was probably easier with a few  treats in their bellies it must have  been weird for the people in the grocery  store to see the cast in descendants  rollin up with a cart full of junk food  water bottle cakes do you guys remember  those awesome Apple cakes that Jay was  doing in descendants two during their  opening number ways to be wicked well  apparently that took some practice it's  harder than it looks  we just found some behind-the-scenes  footage of Jay showing his castmates how  to do that super cool kick move  then it was Sofia's turn she seemed  intimidated at first but connected with  the water bottle on the first try she  didn't seem to realize that she actually  made contact with the bottle  it wasn't until dub yelled you did it  that Sofia knew that she succeeded then  she did a cute victory dance to  celebrate after that dub was next to  give this kick move a try she looked  very sure of herself in the beginning  but she barely tapped the bottle with  her foot causing off-screen hysterical  laughter from a guy we can only assume  with Cameron voice her complete failure  to launch the water bottle didn't stop  her from showing off in a hilarious pose  the next time she tried it she totally  nailed it they have way too much fun for  it to be called a work impressions dub  Cameron and Cameron boys are undeniably  the cutest buddies we've ever seen it's  clear that dub adores Cameron and we're  pretty sure he loves her too like he  would a big sister it makes us that they  would be inseparable given that they  both have history with Disney and know  what it's like more than any of the  other cast members there's a hilarious  behind-the-scenes video of these two  trying to do impressions of each other's  characters and it's awesome first dub  tries to do an impression of Carlos but  she can't because she's laughing too  hard when she finally gets actual words  to come out of her mouth she explains  that his voice goes up and down really  fast  Cameron is laughing so hard at dubs  impression he almost falls over then  Cameron has an impression of now he gets  all emotional and says her line from the  end of the first movie when she says  both of them were rolling on the floor  laughing these two are always having a  blast together better as a villain  can you imagine what The Descendants  movies would have been like if booboo  Stewart had been cast to play the role  of Prince Ben instead of Mitchell hope  well at one time that was a slight  possibility according to an interview  with movie maniacs de bubu originally  auditioned for a different character  than the one he was ultimately cast to  play instead of jubu auditioned to play  the part of Prince Ben he said he went  into auditions countless times over a  period of several months before he  landed the role of Jays we think he's  way better as the sly sword wielding  villain  kid don't you Sophia Carson also  auditioned for a different role at first  to an earlier version of the script had  her reading the part of Gigi the princes  girlfriends we can only assume that  character is now the one we knew as  Audrey can you imagine Audrey's name  being Gigi we think we can speak for  everyone when we say we're glad they  changed it  dov also shared that the name on her  audition script was claudia instead of  now hmm doesn't quite have the same ring  to it does it what was your favorite  descendants behind the scenes moment  tell us in the comments section below  and if you're as excited as we are about  the release of descendants three  subscribe to our channel and give this  video a big thumbs up thanks for  watching the things see you next time  [Music]

